    "body": "Maintainer decisions (question dialog, 2026-11-25) on the design record of PR #4030.\n\nApproved as the record recommends:\n1. The shape of the passes on an Outside start (#3934).\n2. Inside and Outside cut the same passes. Only the order, the start point and the direction change.\n3. Trochoidal is load control. Offset rings and Adaptive stay two choices.\n4. A strategy with load control plans a cut above the limit again. Each cut that stays above the limit has a status line message.\n5. No new material side field on Pocket and 2D Offset.\n6. The code layout: the `path_kernel` folder, and the exit in the entry step.\n\nChanged:\n- The answer on early P1 fixes was: \"Replace the whole motion kernel in one go.\"\n- Scope of the one replacement: 2D milling and 3D Pocket. The other toolpath types stay as they are.\n- Delivery: a side branch and one switch. The program on `main` keeps the old behaviour until the new kernel is proven. No early patch of the P1 faults goes into the old code.\n\nThis replaces decision 5, open question 3 and the migration order of the record. It also replaces the scope line \"2D milling first\" of #4023.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
