    "body": "Maintainer answers (question dialog, 2026-11-25) on the revised record:\n1. The crate name is `camcraft-pathkernel`.\n2. Bore and Thread are in phase 1: yes.\n3. The phase order changes. His words: \"Lathe earlier\", then \"Third\". Phase 2 is sheet cutting, drill and probe. Phase 3 is turning. Then 3D finish, then wire and sinker, then multi-axis.\n4. One issue each for V-Carve, Slot, Trochoidal slot, Slot Undercut and Thread: yes.\n5. A side-branch rule goes into `AGENTS.md` first, and `side/path-kernel` is protected: yes, the two.\n6. The heavy motion and app steps run one time on the side branch before the switch-over: yes.\n7. The maintainer reads the list of changed programs and approves the switch-over PR: yes.\n8. The design is approved. His words: \"Yes, start\".\n\nThe record gets these answers in one more push. Then the new head gets a fresh review, and the PR merges.",
